# H38 mixed versions, run by the implementer (Claude Code, Opus 5.5), 2026-11-23T16:08:56Z, on branch h38-withdraw at 6c0bb13. A listener built at 22791ca (main, before H38) waits for the implementer while commands built at a later commit withdraw a request under the go-ahead and the reviewer then approves it (reviewer-2, #906). The script is evidence/h38/mixed.sh; each command is followed only by what it printed.
## commands built at dc109a9, round 1
$ HANDOFF_ROLE=implementer new post --item W1 --to reviewer --commit A
posted #1 request W1 implementer → reviewer: W1 @ a7868f0001fb
handoff: no session has reviewer now, so this waits until the operator gives one that role; tell the operator.
exit 0
$ (at a terminal) new away "Merge when approved."
away (#2): your go-ahead stands until you run handoff back
Under it, an item is approved once every reviewer it was sent to approves the same commit; one approval is enough for an item sent to one reviewer. handoff doesn't read your words: to tell the agents something without approving anything, use handoff fyi.
No spare: if a seat gets stuck, you'll be told, as now. To have one, start a session and give it the role spare.
not told, no session: implementer, reviewer
no agent has a session now; each session's brief shows your go-ahead when it starts
handoff: told the operator: Your go-ahead is recorded (#2): Merge when approved. Until you run handoff back, items are approved without asking you.
exit 0
$ HANDOFF_ROLE=implementer old wait --timeout 8s &   (the listener built at the old commit, already waiting)
$ HANDOFF_ROLE=implementer new withdraw 1
posted #3 withdraw W1 implementer → reviewer: withdrew #1
exit 0
$ HANDOFF_ROLE=reviewer new reply 1 --verdict APPROVE --commit A
posted #4 reply W1 reviewer → implementer: APPROVE on #1 @ a7868f0001fb
handoff: request #1 was withdrawn by implementer (#3); this reply is recorded and changes nothing
exit 0
the old listener: exit 0 (3 is a timeout), and it printed:
